{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>Mask.</b> Like the form of כסות, and some say like וּבְדַם עֲנָבִים סוּתָה (Genesis 49:11), and do not wonder on account of the vav of מסוה being visible and not so the vav of סותה, for behold עַוְלָתָה (Hosea 10:13) and וְעוֹלָתָה (Job 5:16), עוֹל יָמִים (Isaiah 65:20) and also עֲוִילִים (Job 19:18), אֶל תּוֹךְ הַמַּחֲנֶה (Deuteronomy 23:11), and also וַיְבַתַּר אֹתָם בַּתָּוֶךְ (Genesis 15:10). Some say the light was renewed on Moses' face every time he came to the Tent of Meeting and spoke with HaShem, and he would go out and the light would remain as long as he was speaking to the children of Israel the words of HaShem, and when he finished he would put the mask, for he knew the light would depart and his face return to as it was, and this would be a diminution for Moses if Israel saw his face without light; therefore he would put the mask, and when coming to speak with HaShem he would put the mask to receive the light. And the Gaon [Saadia] said that the light did not depart from his face until the day of his death; therefore his eye did not dim, and this is the correct view—only he said the reason for the mask was lest Israel fear when they quarrel with one another. In my opinion, the mask was there because of the honor of the light that HaShem renewed on his face, so that Israel would not see it at every moment, but only when he spoke to them the words of HaShem, and he would remove the mask when coming to the Tent of Meeting to speak with HaShem face to face; and this is the meaning of ובבא משה."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "I read מסוה as 'mask' following the context of Exodus 34:33–35; the word is debated (veil/mask). The citation Genesis 15:10 is given in the text as 'ברא' טו י' — resolved as Genesis 15:10. The fragmentary final phrase 'וזה טעם ובבא משה' refers to the opening words of the verse being commented on."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:37.591046025Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}